WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.552 --> 00:00:22.433
were three children: Gerald, Jimmy, and Kathleen.

2
00:00:24.474 --> 00:00:27.114
And they were at school in a little town in England.

3
00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:33.216
The boys were at one school, of course, and their sister was at another.

4
00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.990
They used to see each other only on weekends.

5
00:00:39.391 --> 00:00:42.354
So they looked forward to going home for summer vacation.

6
00:00:45.196 --> 00:00:49.800
But one year they couldn't go home because someone in the family had the measles.

7
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.542
That disease was easy to catch.

8
00:00:53.523 --> 00:00:58.747
After many letters back and forth, their parents agreed to let them stay at Kathleen's school.

9
00:01:00.088 --> 00:01:01.409
All the girls had gone home.

10
00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.832
All the teachers had left except the French teacher.

11
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.262
Now the boys had arrived, and they were drinking tea with Kathleen.

12
00:01:09.282 --> 00:01:13.104
"We need a summer project," she said.

13
00:01:13.124 --> 00:01:14.965
"Let's write a book."

14
00:01:16.166 --> 00:01:19.087
"Too much work," said Gerald, who was the oldest.

15
00:01:19.107 --> 00:01:21.309
"We'll do something outdoors.

16
00:01:21.809 --> 00:01:22.669
A cave would be good.

17
00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:24.130
We could eat our meals there."

18
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:28.913
"There aren't any caves," said Jimmy, who liked to say no.

19
00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:33.115
"And I doubt Mademoiselle will let us go out by ourselves."

20
00:01:34.496 --> 00:01:37.169
"Well, I'm going to talk to her," said Gerald.

21
00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.493
He washed his hands and combed his hair before he knocked on Mademoiselle's door.

22
00:01:47.515 --> 00:01:48.235
She was reading.

23
00:01:53.858 --> 00:01:56.260
me, Mademoiselle," said Gerald politely.

24
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.542
"I thought I'd say hello because you're in charge of us."

25
00:02:01.042 --> 00:02:03.744
Mademoiselle was charmed by the young man's manners.

26
00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.165
"Can I do anything for you?"

27
00:02:06.185 --> 00:02:07.926
"No, thank you.

28
00:02:08.406 --> 00:02:09.846
We don't want to be any trouble.

29
00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:14.529
In fact, we would cause less trouble tomorrow if we spent all day outside."

30
00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.150
Mademoiselle smiled.

31
00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.811
"I know what you really want.

32
00:02:20.231 --> 00:02:21.812
You want to be left alone."

33
00:02:22.852 --> 00:02:25.373
Gerald laughed and Mademoiselle did too.

34
00:02:25.393 --> 00:02:28.095
"Go ahead," she said.

35
00:02:28.115 --> 00:02:30.676
"I won't stand in your way."

36
00:02:32.268 --> 00:02:35.309
The next morning the children went off on their adventure.

37
00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.670
It was a beautiful day.

38
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.292
"We're sure to find something," said Gerald.

39
00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:44.913
"A boy at school said that there was a cave near here.

40
00:02:45.313 --> 00:02:47.434
But he said there's an enchanted castle too.

41
00:02:47.954 --> 00:02:49.455
So none of that may be true."

42
00:02:50.976 --> 00:02:53.997
The children walked along the road, which was very hot.

43
00:02:54.897 --> 00:02:57.178
They decided to share a drink from their lunch.

44
00:02:58.258 --> 00:03:00.159
Soon they came to a fork in the road.

45
00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:04.557
They went right and came to another fork and then another.

46
00:03:04.577 --> 00:03:08.400
"We're completely lost," said Kathleen.

47
00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.201
"What fun!"

48
00:03:15.724 --> 00:03:20.066
Now the trees arched overhead and bushes lined the banks along the road.

49
00:03:20.086 --> 00:03:23.288
"Let's have some lunch," said Jimmy.

50
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:27.210
As they sat down, Gerald leaned against some bushes.

51
00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.651
"Oh my!"

52
00:03:30.112 --> 00:03:30.612
he cried.

53
00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:35.114
The bushes gave way and he almost fell backward.

54
00:03:35.974 --> 00:03:37.815
The other two pulled back the bushes.

55
00:03:38.736 --> 00:03:40.537
There was a large hole in the bank.

56
00:03:40.557 --> 00:03:42.338
"It's a cave!"

57
00:03:42.918 --> 00:03:43.618
said Gerald.

58
00:03:43.638 --> 00:03:45.099
"I'm going in."

59
00:03:45.119 --> 00:03:47.120
"Oh, don't!"

60
00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:48.441
said Kathleen.

61
00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.602
"There might be snakes."

62
00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:54.064
But Gerald was already crawling through the hole.

63
00:03:54.084 --> 00:03:56.605
"It is a cave!

64
00:03:57.026 --> 00:03:57.566
Come look!"

65
00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.948
Kathleen and Jimmy followed him down the hole.

66
00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.281
They walked a short distance and came out into the sunshine.

67
00:04:05.301 --> 00:04:07.942
"How wonderful!"

68
00:04:08.523 --> 00:04:09.363
said Kathleen.

69
00:04:10.363 --> 00:04:14.005
Ahead of them was a tall arch framed with ferns and grasses.

70
00:04:14.025 --> 00:04:19.627
"It looks like a train tunnel," said Jimmy.

71
00:04:19.647 --> 00:04:24.789
"It's the entrance to the enchanted castle," said Kathleen.

72
00:04:24.809 --> 00:04:26.850
"Oh, don't be silly."

73
00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.051
Gerald led the way to the arch.

74
00:04:29.071 --> 00:04:31.432
"There's a set of steps!"

75
00:04:32.032 --> 00:04:32.672
said Jimmy.

76
00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:38.154
They followed Gerald down the steps, walking slowly through the darkness.

77
00:04:39.134 --> 00:04:40.954
Up ahead was a patch of daylight.

78
00:04:41.875 --> 00:04:45.616
The children passed under another arch and out onto a terrace.

79
00:04:47.076 --> 00:04:49.257
Below them was a lake with an island.

80
00:04:50.197 --> 00:04:53.598
Beyond that, marble statues gleamed among the trees.

81
00:04:55.498 --> 00:04:57.859
White towers stood out against the sky.

82
00:04:57.879 --> 00:05:00.840
"It's the enchanted castle!"

83
00:05:01.141 --> 00:05:02.026
cried Kathleen.
